**An electric-drive dump truck comprising:**

a vehicle body supported by a plurality of wheels;

at least one electric traction motor operatively coupled to one or more of the plurality of wheels;

a pair of electrical power collection units movably mounted to the vehicle body and configured, when in a raised position, to contact respective conductors of an external electrical power supply and deliver electrical power to the at least one electric traction motor;

respective lifting devices operatively coupled to the electrical power collection units and controllable to move the electrical power collection units between the raised position and a lowered position;

a position-detection device comprising a global positioning system receiver and configured to generate position information indicative of a geographic position of the dump truck;

a speed sensor configured to generate speed information indicative of a travel speed of the dump truck;

a storage device storing route information identifying one or more locations at which raising of the electrical power collection units is permitted; and

a controller communicatively coupled to the lifting devices, the position-detection device, the speed sensor, and the storage device,

wherein the controller is configured to:

determine, based at least in part on the position information and the stored route information, a distance from the dump truck to a location at which raising of the electrical power collection units is permitted;

predict, based at least in part on the determined distance and the speed information, whether the dump truck will satisfy a predetermined collector-raising condition; and

permit or command the lifting devices to raise the electrical power collection units in response to predicting that the predetermined collector-raising condition will be satisfied.

The predetermined collector-raising condition may include at least one of the dump truck being within a prescribed geographic region, traveling below a threshold speed, traveling in an authorized direction, being aligned with the external electrical power supply, or being predicted to enter a power-collection zone within a predetermined time interval. The controller may inhibit raising of the electrical power collection units when the predetermined collector-raising condition is not satisfied and may lower the electrical power collection units upon detecting or predicting departure from the power-collection zone.
